            <ArticleTitle>[Functional metabolic activity of leukocytes in myocardial infarct].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>79 myocardial infarction (MI) patients exhibited enhanced activity of myeloperoxidase and high levels of cation protein in leukocytes. These indices rose to maximal and recovered on the disease days 5-7 and 30-40, respectively. Intracellular components of leukocytes in acute MI patients changed in accordance with the stage and severity of the pathological process. This provides additional information on MI prognosis and aftercare efficiency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
